request.description:
The service resolves the seed host and refuses anything on a private, loopback or link-local address, so an unauthenticated caller cannot use it to reach inside the network. privateSeed holds the address to try. The CLI has no such guard, because your own terminal already reaches those.

---

### Example responses, captured from a live run

**422 private address**

```json
{
  "detail": {
    "seed": "169.254.169.254 is a private address"
  }
}
```

